==English==

===Etymology===
[[remarkable]] + [[-ly]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-remarkably.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# {{context|manner|lang=en}} In a [[remarkable]] manner.
#: ''He performed the piece '''remarkably''', offering novel interpretations to its nearly cliched passages.''
# {{context|degree|lang=en}} To a [[noteworthy]] extent.
#: ''That dog is '''remarkably''' fierce.''
#*{{quote-news|year=2013|date=April 9|author=Andrei Lankov|title=Stay Cool. Call North Korea’s Bluff.|work=New York Times|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/opinion/stay-cool-call-north-koreas-bluff.html?_r=0
|passage=Suggestions that those leaders are irrational and their decisions unfathomable are '''remarkably''' shallow. North Korea is not a theocracy led by zealots who preach the rewards of the afterlife.}}
# {{context|evaluative|lang=en}} {{non-gloss definition|Used to draw special attention to a proposition}}.
#: '''''Remarkably''', three State assembly elections were decided by a total of fewer than one hundred votes.''

